    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nConsolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived **`identityKey`** = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`. A create request is now rejected with **409 only when the new owner's whole identity key matches an existing owner's**.\n\n### New code\n- **`IdentityKey`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 the single definition of the key, built from an owner's already-canonical stored fields (E.164 telephone, lower-cased email, household id). Used by both the check and the response mapper, so they can't drift.\n- **`EnsureUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 the one duplicate step: computes the built owner's key and compares it against every existing owner's key.\n- **`DuplicateIdentityException`** + handler + escalation YAML \u2014 the 409 (mirrors the old handlers, reusing `ProblemDetails`).\n\n### Wiring\n- `owners.POST.yml`: dropped `EnsureUniqueTelephone` / `EnsureUniqueEmail` / `EnsureUniqueHousehold`; inserted `ensureUniqueIdentity` **after `assignHousehold`**. Placement matters: `AssignHousehold` settles the new owner's and any linked members' `householdId`, so both sides of the comparison are compared in their final form. This is why two members of the same household with different telephones get different keys and are both allowed, while an exact full-key match is caught.\n\n### Response\n- Added `identityKey` (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` and mapped it in `OwnerMapper` via `IdentityKey.of(owner)`, so the endpoint returns it.\n\n### Cleanup\n- Deleted the three old `EnsureUnique*` functions, the three `Duplicate*Exception`/handler pairs, and their escalation YAMLs; updated stale javadoc references in `E164Telephone` and `Household` to point at `IdentityKey`.\n\n**Test result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` (same telephone \u2192 409) passes, full build green.",
